1
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,120
This is how I'll become.

2
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,600
This is how I'll become.

3
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,000
Supreme Commander!

4
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,580
A hero!

5
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:24,200
This is my story!

6
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,760
In the dark darkness,

7
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:37,400
I'm one and one, I'm one and one,

8
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,936
I'm tired of crying!

9
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,800
I'm a dream of a dream?

10
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,420
But now, when I was your
friend, I would bring you back.

11
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,940
I'm not always gonna go up here,

12
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:27,800
but I don't want to be the only one.

13
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,840
I'll be the only one.

14
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:33,477
I'll be the only one that
I'll be the only one day.

15
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:34,537
I'll be the only one day long.

16
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:37,677
Please don't go anywhere,
fast, then share me the world.

17
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,231
Let's make the new world.

18
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:40,370
I'll never experience the world.

19
00:01:40,453 --> 00:01:41,829
We will be the only world.

20
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,700
I've got this!

21
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:26,520
Nice one, Commander!

22
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,390
Boom!

23
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,740
I'm very disappointed.

24
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:49,260
I waited patiently, yet only
two targets came out to play.

25
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,240
Where are the rest of you?

26
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,841
Two targets with myself included.

27
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:56,028
Is he after the commanders?

28
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,557
This fight will be over.

29
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,680
In the mere blink of an eye!

30
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:12,500
That was the strength of their leader?

31
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:16,200
I expected more from those little pests.

32
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:24,287
If you could stay still,
that would be great.

33
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,440
You dare attempt to kick me?

34
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,917
How arrogant of you!

35
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,360
My flesh is as strong as steel.

36
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:31,580
Now block this!

37
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:34,640
I am invincible!

38
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,920
I'm hurt? Impossible.

39
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:49,950
Incredible.

40
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,720
She's taking on a humanoid.

41
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,780
Lady 10 is very talented.

42
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,865
She can escape anything
because of her ability.

43
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,471
but she doesn't actually need to run away.

44
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:05,037
Both commanders came up with a plan to
wipe out an invading army in no time flat,

45
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,837
and they did it all in their heads!

46
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,860
Oh my god, Lady Ken!

47
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:11,120
Lady Ken, you're so freaking hot!

48
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:12,480
Oh my god!

49
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,130
Grat!

50
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,600
All right, fine!

51
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:22,037
Well, this time I'll simply have to...

52
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,560
blow you to pieces!

53
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:28,830
Ha ha ha!

54
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,900
Ha ha ha ha ha!

55
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,740
Good luck avoiding that one!

56
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:37,720
What? Is she?

57
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Just relax.

58
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:41,320
That's the end of her.

59
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,190
Huh?

60
00:04:44,273 --> 00:04:46,142
Did he really think it was over?

61
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:58,560
She teleported me by tossing me?

62
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,080
The perfect decision.

63
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:12,717
Lady Ten has the godlike ability to
manipulate space around her, aptly named...

64
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,100
Ame no mitori.

65
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:35,880
If I rip apart the fabric of space,
your defenses don't do you much good.

66
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,940
An entire swarm of Shuki gone.

67
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,877
All of the commanders
are brilliant like that.

68
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,254
They're obviously on a different level.

69
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:49,641
And Miss Kyoka wants to be the
Supreme Commander in charge of them?

70
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,495
Sounds like an awfully ambitious goal.

71
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:59,160
True, but I'm going to be the
next Supreme Commander in line.

72
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,205
I guess I don't have to worry.

73
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:05,597
All right, hunt the
stragglers and take them out!

74
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,510
Yes, ma 'am!

75
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:11,817
I can't just stand around
gawking at Miss Kyoka.

76
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:15,260
I made up my mind to be a hero in Mato!

77
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,660
We exterminated the Shuki army.

78
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:30,897
But according to Nei's report, there
were other enemy generals present.

79
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,837
And yet there was no sign of them.

80
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:36,657
We searched as thorough as possible,
but still came up empty-handed.

81
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:40,217
Maybe what happened is all of them
got squashed in that big blast.

82
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:41,580
I'm not so sure.

83
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:43,312
They were very peculiar.

84
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,780
I'm sorry, everyone.

85
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:50,620
Even with the power of foresight,
I detected the enemy too late.

86
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,860
Hey, it happens.

87
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,797
They probably used some
sort of cloaking ability.

88
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:58,597
You detected them before
they started attacking us.

89
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:02,060
Meaning, you circumvented
any potential for an ambush.

90
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:05,516
You did your job well, so
don't dwell on the negative.

91
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,220
Precisely. Yay!

92
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:12,460
Little Slave, You really
stole the show out there.

93
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:14,547
Oh, I don't know about that.

94
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:17,702
You were way more impressive
than me, Miss Izumo.

95
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:19,380
Mr. Yuki!

96
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:22,237
I witnessed your performance
on the battlefield!

97
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,297
So now I know that boys can
be talented sometimes too!

98
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:27,877
If you don't mind, can
I have your autograph?

99
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:28,790
Me?

100
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:30,840
You see, now you've got a fan.

101
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,230
Hey.

102
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,960
What do you want?

103
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,340
About earlier.

104
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,146
Thank you for saving my life.

105
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:44,957
Yeah, well, you are an Azuma.

106
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:48,937
If I'd let the enemy defeat you, it
would bring shame upon the family.

107
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:50,837
That is the only reason why I saved you.

108
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:54,837
Of course, if you're saying that you
felt the weight of your own inadequacies.

109
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,897
I'd graciously train them out of you.

110
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,460
So come back home and.

111
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,920
The 7th Squadron is my home.

112
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:07,597
Writing up a report is
going to be a challenge.

113
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,197
As for the exhibition match...

114
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,110
Mm-hmm.

115
00:08:10,193 --> 00:08:11,837
I suppose we'll call it a draw for now.

116
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,920
It's unfortunate.

117
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,577
I was really looking
forward to our one-on-one.

118
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:16,600
Yes, me too.

119
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,417
Well, we'll be heading out now.

120
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:20,560
Bye-bye, ladies!

121
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:23,500
See you later.

122
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:34,320
Well I'm beat I need a
nice refreshing bath.

123
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:43,200
Is this supposed to be my reward
weren't you the one who asked for this?

124
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:48,520
So indecent well he did slay a
substantial number of Shuuki today.

125
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:50,800
Miss Kyoka too?

126
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:53,200
I get both at the same time?

127
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:55,126
It's the price of my ability.

128
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,800
Every single time.

129
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:59,500
Yet I'm always surprised. Wait a minute.

130
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:04,280
She's going to get in
the hot spring with me?

131
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,560
Freaking pervert.

132
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,428
Take off your damn clothes!

133
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,738
Oh, uh, yes ma 'am!

134
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:21,157
I wasn't exactly sure what to
expect when we stripped down naked,

135
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:23,697
but evidently he wanted a good scrap down.

136
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:27,017
I just thought it would be kind
of nice to freshen up a little.

137
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:29,397
Well, it's basically the
same thing as bathing a dog,

138
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:31,157
so there's no reason to be embarrassed.

139
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:34,769
I can't understand anything you
say when you talk that fast.

140
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:39,320
Yuki, your body is more
tired than usual, isn't it?

141
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,060
Mm, it is.

142
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,772
Two masters at once took a lot out of me.

143
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,414
So it makes you strong, but
it's not to be used lightly.

144
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:48,350
Right.

145
00:09:48,433 --> 00:09:51,017
We learned to utilize the
skill in a practical way,

146
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:55,218
and we'll need to continue to explore
its possibilities in the future.

147
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:59,337
But for the time being,
you should get some rest.

148
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:02,361
The dorm's hot spring is
great for curing fatigue.

149
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,620
The lens naysaw!

150
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:15,760
Look like this!

151
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,420
It's amazing as always!

152
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,300
My magnum opus!

153
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:26,517
Sure, it's good, but the
art style is kind of...

154
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,600
They'll make an official
composite sketch at HQ later on.

155
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:35,220
Neither of them are the humanoid
we encountered last time.

156
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:52,197
The one that looks like my sister
how come she wasn't with them?

157
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:54,537
Maybe they're a different squad

158
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:59,360
or is there some other reason?

159
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,720
Oh, my God.

160
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:38,936
So this is the Sixth Squadron's dorm.

161
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:42,117
All of the dormitories look
identical on the outside.

162
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:45,077
I noticed that when we
visited the Fifth Squadron.

163
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,760
For the most part, yes.

164
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,687
Though the interiors
tend to differ slightly.

165
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,259
Welcome to the Sixth Squadron dorm.

166
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,977
Thanks for making the trek.

167
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:57,354
A little change of scenery never hurts.

168
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:00,917
Did he run into any
trouble on your way over?

169
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,617
Took down some Shuki in
route, but that's it.

170
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,641
It was business as usual in Mato.

171
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,777
Tenka and I need to have a meeting.

172
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,840
For now, these are my orders.

173
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:15,397
Get properly acquainted
with the Sixth Squadron.

174
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:19,177
A few members went out on an
expedition, so they won't be joining us.

175
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,617
But the rest of the girls
are still here in the dorm,

176
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,577
so feel free to take a look around.

177
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,490
Thank you.

178
00:12:24,573 --> 00:12:27,380
And Yuki, as we discussed
this morning... Yes.

179
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:31,346
As the 7th Squad's caretaker, I
will help out in any way I can.

180
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:34,997
Unfortunately, our caretaker
isn't available at the moment.

181
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:37,217
It's just until they return this evening.

182
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:38,130
My apologies.

183
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:39,460
Not a problem.

184
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,857
As part of the Demon Defense Force,
we've got to have each other's backs.

185
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:43,777
Wouldn't you agree?

186
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:44,690
Right.

187
00:12:44,773 --> 00:12:46,112
I'll be counting on you.

188
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,010
Uh...

189
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:50,330
Right!

190
00:12:50,413 --> 00:12:51,243
Leave it to me!

191
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,040
All right, first things first, cleaning.

192
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:01,520
Or it would be.

193
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:04,240
But this place is pretty clean already.

194
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:08,680
And here I was getting all amped up.

195
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,640
Hm? Oh.

196
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:12,700
This stain.

197
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:15,489
Judging by the feel of it,

198
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:19,097
Formula 5 might work better
than just plain old baking soda.

199
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:21,677
Hmm, or maybe...

200
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:23,300
So many choices!

201
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,940
Next up is laundry!

202
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:33,570
Breathe.

203
00:13:33,653 --> 00:13:34,483
Just breathe.

204
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:37,880
You do the 7th Squad's
laundry all the time.

205
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,140
Never mind.

206
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:42,000
I'm still not used to it.

207
00:13:44,940 --> 00:13:47,480
I wonder what Yuki is up to right now.

208
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:51,380
Oh man, I wish I could have gone with him.

209
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,540
I told myself I'd get him to like me more.

210
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:03,427
If anything, I should be using
this time for self-improvement.

211
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:08,800
I guess I'll start by tidying up.

212
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:15,720
Himari's big sister's room.

213
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,731
I wonder what she'll say when she sees me.

214
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:27,860
Anyone home?

215
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:31,710
Hello?

216
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:35,880
She's not here.

217
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:38,612
I guess I'll just leave this in her room.

218
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:39,900
Pardon me?

219
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,330
What the...

220
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,790
Sahara Wakasa?

221
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,736
Why is she asleep in the living room?

222
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:17,420
And in her underwear, no less.

223
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:22,900
I can't let her catch
a cold, so I'll just...

224
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,320
Does she think I'm her pillow?

225
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,660
I have to bail before someone sees me.

226
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:42,920
No, no, you're not going anyway. Oh, yeah.

227
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:47,237
This is the girl who wrestled like
a pro in the exhibition match.

228
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,600
Either way, I've got to get free.

229
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:51,740
Now behave yourself.

230
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:59,860
And though I wished for
escape, I was unable to escape.

231
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:04,600
So, eventually, I stopped
thinking and gave in.

232
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,940
Aw, sorry, my bad.

233
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:14,140
I completely forgot the 7th Squadron
was supposed to come visit today. Yeah.

234
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:15,850
Huh?

235
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:19,320
Hey, Himari, what's up?

236
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:22,387
I'm waiting until she's
done to speak to her.

237
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:42,380
Does Yachiho do this regularly? Mm-hmm.

238
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:45,955
She trained like that before
the exhibition match, too.

239
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:48,609
She's pushing herself
even harder nowadays.

240
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:52,420
Hey, do you look up to Yachi?

241
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:55,288
I mean, since she's
your big sister and all.

242
00:16:56,380 --> 00:17:01,620
Her personality is terrible, but she's
successful academically and athletically.

243
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:05,452
I've always thought I could
learn a thing or two from her.

244
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:06,810
Personally,

245
00:17:06,893 --> 00:17:09,837
I'm a fan of the theory that
someone's Peach ability is

246
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:13,177
based on their human nature
and knowledge they've acquired.

247
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:14,540
So in your case,

248
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:19,447
your desire to learn from Yachi is the
reason why learning became your ability.

249
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:22,679
And the same goes for Yachi's
skill to control time.

250
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:26,567
It stems from her desire to spend
time with her little sister.

251
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,426
Makes sense, don't you think?

252
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:29,450
Hmm.

253
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:32,957
I think that you are making
a lot of assumptions.

254
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:37,680
Aw, but it might be nice if you talk
to her a little more often, right?

255
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,400
Huh? Yeah.

256
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,817
Your big sister's cool.

257
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:48,080
Here I guess she is.

258
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:09,257
What can't hear you you
need to check your attitude!

259
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:13,420
What a relief looks like they're
getting along better already? Yeah.

260
